{"id": 47, "ts": 1779720822.3130283, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I remain convinced that **Candidate\u202fC** is the stronger overall fit.\u202fWhile Agent\u202f2 rightly points out the lack of direct evidence on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision\u2011making in high\u2011pressure scenarios, we do have concrete evidence for Candidate\u202fC: he \u201cmakes correct decisions quickly,\u201d which directly addresses decision quality and suggests the ability to act decisively under stress.\u202fCombined with his 100\u202f% reliability, the positive atmosphere he creates with the crew, and his excellent attention skills, C covers the core safety pillars of reliability, decision quality, and crew cooperation.\u202fHis noted difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric perception are concerns, but the existing note that he \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew\u201d indicates that these traits have not yet manifested as a crew\u2011resource\u2011management problem.\u202fIn contrast, B\u2019s interpersonal drawbacks (grumpy, uncooperative) directly threaten crew cooperation, and we still lack evidence of his decision quality under severe conditions.\u202fTherefore, I keep my vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
